# Caddy in front of FerrumPix (see docker-compose.yml next to it). Caddy gets the certificate for
# FERRUMPIX_DOMAIN by itself, as long as that name points at this computer from the internet and
# the ports 80 and 443 are reachable.
#
# Only in your own network, without a public name: uncomment the line "tls internal". Caddy then
# issues its own certificate, which the browser has to trust once.
#
# Caddy sets X-Forwarded-Proto and X-Forwarded-Host itself and passes the WebSocket under /ws
# through without further settings. The address is the fixed one of FerrumPix in the Compose
# network.

{$FERRUMPIX_DOMAIN} {
	# tls internal
	reverse_proxy 172.30.145.3:14500
}
